   {
    "name": "_get_welcome_steps",
    "kind": "preparation_rule",
    "arguments": [
     "self"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "im_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": "Returns a sub-set of script_step_ids that only contains the \"welcoming steps\".\nWe consider those as all the steps the bot will say before expecting a first answer from\nthe end user.\n\nExample 1:\n- step 1 (question_selection): What do you want to do? - Create a Lead, -Create a Ticket\n- step 2 (text): Thank you for visiting our website!\n-> The welcoming steps will only contain step 1, since directly after that we expect an\ninput from the user\n\nExample 2:\n- step 1 (text): Hello! I'm a bot!\n- step 2 (text): I am here to help lost users.\n- step 3 (question_selection): What do you want to do? - Create a Lead, -Create a Ticket\n- step 4 (text): Thank you for visiting our website!\n-> The welcoming steps will contain steps 1, 2 and 3.\nMeaning the bot will have a small monologue with himself before expecting an input from the\nend user.\n\nThis is important because we need to display those welcoming steps in a special fashion on\nthe frontend, since those are not inserted into the discuss.channel as actual mail.messages,\nto avoid bloating the channels with bot messages if the end-user never interacts with it. ",
      "size_in_lines": 32,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": []
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "name": "_post_welcome_steps",
    "kind": "internal_rule",
    "arguments": [
     "self",
     "discuss_channel"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "im_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": "Welcome messages are only posted after the visitor's first interaction with the chatbot.\nSee 'chatbot.script#_get_welcome_steps()' for more details.\n\nSide note: it is important to set the 'chatbot_current_step_id' on each iteration so that\nit's correctly set when going into 'discuss_channel#_message_post_after_hook()'. ",
      "size_in_lines": 22,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": []
     }
    ]
   },
